[method]
The paper describes AF2Complex, an AlphaFold2-based protein-complex structure prediction workflow. It predicts three-dimensional complex conformations from multimeric sequence inputs and evaluates them on CASP14 multimeric targets, including the case studies CcmEFH and CcmFGH. The workflow also uses an interface clash indicator to assess interface quality and applies statistical tests to compare AF2Complex against docking-centric structure-prediction approaches. This is directly related to the proposed research method because both aim to infer protein-complex architecture from sequence-level information; the paper uses an AlphaFold2-based method on curated CASP14 targets, whereas the research plan proposes using AlphaFold 3 to predict complexes such as photosystem I and II components from single-organism transcriptomic data.
